<title>UK: Shell up after upbeat company presentation.</title>
<headline>Shell up after upbeat company presentation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc rose 19 pence to 1174-1/2 after an upbeat company presentation at an industry analyst conference here on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>NatWest Markets reiterated its positive stance on the shares following the presentation by Royal Dutch/Shell Group managing director Cor Herkstroter, dealers added.</p>
<p>Herkstroter spoke at the conference organised by the National Association of Petroleum Investment Analysts from the U.S.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
